
Fix the lifecycle cleanup gap when configuration
loading fails during a TestNG setup callback.

Requirements:

1. Reproduce the failure with a real TestNG
   7.12.0 integration test using a missing
   environment configuration file.

2. Inspect which lifecycle callbacks actually
   execute when setup throws an exception.

3. Ensure that every activation created by the
   adapter is closed, even if setup fails before
   the normal cleanup callback.

4. Ensure that failed or abandoned invocation
   contexts are eventually released safely.

5. Never release a context while a valid
   activation is still using it.

6. Preserve the original configuration exception.
   Cleanup failures must not hide the root cause.

7. Ensure subsequent tests on the same thread
   cannot inherit stale context bindings.

8. Preserve correct behavior for parallel tests,
   retries and skipped tests.

9. Reuse the existing coordinator, lifecycle
   manager and invocation tracker.

10. Do not introduce global mutable state or
    redesign the configuration engine.

11. Preserve all public APIs and signatures.

12. Keep the core independent of TestNG.

Add focused regression tests and execute the
complete Maven reactor.

Report the exact test results and any remaining
cleanup risks.

Keep the production changes minimal.










